    <!-- "(HEAD)" is not decoration. libXray v26.7.11's MeasureDelay hardcodes an
         HTTP HEAD, so a GET-based "proxy" mode does not exist and a provider's
         `ping-type: proxy` resolves to this. Do not shorten to "Proxy" — that
         would promise a request this build cannot make. -->
    <string name="settings_ping_mode_proxy_head">Proxy (HEAD)</string>
    <string name="settings_ping_mode_tcp_summary">Real round-trip to the server. Fast, works for every protocol, and comparable with other clients. Does not prove the proxy itself works.</string>
    <string name="settings_ping_mode_proxy_head_summary">Sends a request through the proxy. Much slower, and proves the server actually carries traffic.</string>
